      ['Which gas does the circulation bring to the muscles?', 'oxygen', [['carbon dioxide', 'Muscles give that one off. 💨'], ['nitrogen', 'It goes in and out of the lungs unused. 🌬️'], ['helium', 'It makes your voice squeaky, not your legs faster. 🎈']], 'Muscles use oxygen and nutrients to release energy.'],
      ['Which gas do we breathe out in greater amounts?', 'carbon dioxide', [['oxygen', 'That is the one we keep most of. 🫁'], ['ozone', 'It is mostly high up in the atmosphere. ☁️'], ['helium', 'No. 🎈']], 'Exhaled air has more CO₂ and less oxygen than inhaled air.'],
      ['Where do gas exchanges take place in the lungs?', 'in the alveoli', [['in the windpipe', 'The windpipe carries air; it exchanges nothing. 🌬️'], ['in the nose', 'The nose filters and warms the air. 👃'], ['in the stomach', 'It digests; it does not breathe. 🍽️']], 'Alveoli have a very thin wall surrounded by capillaries.'],
      ['Which organ drives the circulation?', 'the heart', [['the liver', 'The liver stores and processes substances. 🟤'], ['the lungs', 'They exchange gases. 🫁'], ['the brain', 'It gives orders; it does not pump. 🧠']], 'The heart is a hollow muscle that works like a pump.'],
      ['What happens during exercise?', 'heart rate and breathing speed up', [['the heart slows down', 'The opposite: it speeds up. 🏃'], ['we breathe less', 'We breathe faster and deeper. 🌬️'], ['nothing changes', 'Your heart would disagree. ❤️']], 'Muscles need more oxygen and nutrients.'],
      ['Which sense organ picks up sounds?', 'the ear', [['the eye', 'The eye picks up light. 👁️'], ['the tongue', 'The tongue picks up tastes. 👅'], ['the skin', 'The skin picks up touch, heat and cold. ✋']], 'Sense organs turn a stimulus into a nerve message.'],
      ['How do messages travel between the brain and the muscles?', 'through nerves (nerve messages)', [['through the bones', 'Bones support the body. 🦴'], ['through the digestive tract', 'It deals with food. 🍽️'], ['through the air', 'No airmail inside the body. 🌬️']], 'Sense organ → nerve → brain → nerve → muscle.'],
      ['What is puberty?', 'the period when the body becomes able to reproduce', [['birth', 'Puberty comes much later. 👶'], ['old age', 'Far too late! 👵'], ['an illness', 'It is a normal stage of life. 🌱']], 'At puberty, the reproductive organs start working.'],
      ['What are the reproductive cells called?', 'sperm cells and egg cells', [['red and white cells', 'Those are cells of the circulation. 🔴'], ['neurons', 'Those are nerve cells. 🧠'], ['alveoli', 'Those are tiny air sacs in the lungs. 🫁']], 'Fertilisation: a sperm cell joins an egg cell.'],
      ['How can we limit the spread of germs every day?', 'wash our hands and get vaccinated', [['never sleep', 'Sleep actually helps the body. 😴'], ['eat lots of sugar', 'That does not stop germs. 🍬'], ['stop drinking water', 'Drinking water is essential. 💧']], 'Hygiene, vaccination and antiseptics limit infections.']
